From 2ac48432dc2f22f261f4893c236c51ab1088ea19 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 23:10:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] sha256: keep the target CPU when enabling the crypto
 extensions

On AArch64, "arch=armv8-a+crypto" replaces the -mcpu/-march of the
build with plain Armv8.0-A. For -mcpu=cortex-a53 this drops CRC, and GCC
then refuses to inline always_inline functions compiled for the full
target, such as a fortified memset():

  error: inlining failed in call to 'always_inline' 'memset':
  target specific option mismatch

Use "+crypto" on AArch64, as aesce.c does, which adds the extension to
the build target. Keep "arch=armv8-a+crypto" for AArch32.

Link: https://github.com/Mbed-TLS/mbedtls/pull/10986
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
---
--- a/library/sha256.c
+++ b/library/sha256.c
@@ -102,7 +102,11 @@
 #          error "A more recent GCC is required for MBEDTLS_SHA256_USE_ARMV8_A_CRYPTO_*"
 #        else
 #          pragma GCC push_options
-#          pragma GCC target ("arch=armv8-a+crypto")
+#          if defined(MBEDTLS_ARCH_IS_ARM64)
+#            pragma GCC target ("+crypto")
+#          else
+#            pragma GCC target ("arch=armv8-a+crypto")
+#          endif
 #          define MBEDTLS_POP_TARGET_PRAGMA
 #        endif
 #      else
